en.player_ai_control:
Player character: {name}
{setting}
AI may write new dialogue and replies for {name}, using ordinary dialog items with non-empty speech, just like other characters. Do not output only empty portrait items or repeat the user's words this turn. Do not decide key actions or major choices for the user. Use {portrait_field} to select the player's expression; portrait-only items use {portrait_value} and empty speech. The user's explicit words, actions, and corrections take precedence.

en.player_control:
User-controlled player character: {name}
{setting}
The user's message contains words, deliberate actions, and explicit thoughts already supplied for {name}. Never invent dialogue, answers, key actions, or choices for {name}, including through narration, indirect speech, or another character. After another character asks a question or presents a choice, wait for the user.
When the player's expression changes, add a normal dialog item before other characters: {{"character_name":"{name}","{portrait_field}":"{portrait_value}","speech":""}}. This item updates the player portrait and is not visible dialogue; omit it when the expression does not change. {speech_contract}
Narration involving the player should name {name}. CHOICE entries are suggestions not yet performed.

en.self_persona_block:
[User Persona]
{setting}
(The above describes the background and preferences of the user conversing with you; naturally incorporate it in interaction, and do not output "Self Persona" as a standalone speaking character.)

en.xml_player_ai_control:
Player character: {name}
{setting}
AI may write new dialogue and replies for {name} using ordinary <say char="{name}" {portrait_field}="...">line</say> tags. Do not repeat the user's input or decide key choices for them. To update portrait expression without spoken dialogue, use a self-closing <say char="{name}" {portrait_field}="{portrait_value}" /> tag. User words, actions, and corrections always take priority.

en.xml_player_control:
User-controlled player character: {name}
{setting}
User messages represent words, deliberate actions, and explicit thoughts already supplied by {name}. Never invent lines, answers, key actions, or choices for {name}, even via narration or other characters. Wait for the user after questions or choices.
To update the player's expression alone, emit a self-closing tag before other characters: <say char="{name}" {portrait_field}="{portrait_value}" /> (portrait only, omit if unchanged). {speech_contract}
Name {name} explicitly in <narr> when needed; <choice> suggestions do not represent actions already taken.

